<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - June 13.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - June 13.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Tyson Foods Inc said it does not expect to meet Wall Street estimates for fiscal third-quarter earnings because of operating and margin pressures.</p>
<p>-- PacifiCorp said it would acquire Britain's Energy Group Plc for $9.6 billion. PacifiCorp said it would sell its Pacific Telecom unit for $1.5 billion as part of the deal.</p>
<p>-- Mitchell Energy &amp; Development Corp said it agreed to sell Woodlands Corp for $543 million to a partnership of Morgan Stanley Real Estate Fund II LP and Crescent Real Estate Equities.</p>
</text>
